text:
Now the question: "most matches in the 2008/2009 season". L2 says MAX(league_name WHERE season='2008/2009'), i.e., count matches per league for that season, take the max. Note there may be a tie — the all-time question had a 3-way tie. Let's check.

SQL: SELECT League.name, COUNT(*) FROM Match JOIN League ON Match.league_id = League.id WHERE Match.season = '2008/2009' GROUP BY League.id ORDER BY COUNT(*) DESC;

Note: the season format in this DB is '2008/2009'. Let's run and check for ties.
